.claude/

# logbook recorder — host-matched ffmpeg and content-hashed narration clips are
# machine-/content-specific, provisioned by `logbook --setup`; don't commit them.
.armada/logbook/bin/
.armada/logbook/cache/

# cartographer — per-repo learned heuristics are local working state, not part of
# the distributed plugin; keep ARMADA's own cartography out of the product repo.
.armada/cartography/

# foghorn — hash-cached spoken clips are machine-/content-specific scratch, keyed
# by (text + voice + provider); regenerated on demand, never part of the plugin.
.armada/foghorn/cache/

# foghorn — the repo-local .env supplies the cloud-voice SECRET (e.g.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY) and any FOGHORN_* per-repo, without depending on OS env
# propagation. It is a secret-bearing file — NEVER commit it. (foghorn-say.mjs
# loads .armada/foghorn/.env then repo-root .env without overriding real env.)
.armada/foghorn/.env
/.env

# spyglass cost post-mortem — the per-run token/cost breakdown crows-nest writes
# at its reconcile points (crows-nest §8g), plus the run→(branch,worktree) map the
# read-only dashboard consumes. Machine-/run-specific scratch, regenerated live from
# real usage; the read-only driver only READS it. NEVER commit it (out of the tracked
# tree by design — the producer writes ONLY under out/costs/).
out/costs/

# fleet liveness beats — the per-run phase/step heartbeat + terminal marker that
# shipwright/muster subagents emit (scripts/liveness-beat.mjs) so crows-nest can
# tell working / done / wedged apart instead of guessing on output-file mtime
# (crows-nest §2d, issue #134). Machine-/run-specific scratch, regenerated live;
# the reader only READS it. NEVER commit it (out of the tracked tree by design —
# the producer writes ONLY under out/liveness/).
out/liveness/
